1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 10=

3
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:18,580
Here.

4
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:27,550
Zicheng.

5
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,800
I'm leaving.

6
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:30,230
Stay safe.

7
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:30,680
Okay.

8
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,670
Here are the application materials
I've put together.

9
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,910
I hope to see you
at Hua University next year.

10
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:25,240
Senior.

11
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:26,800
I have a gift for you, too.

12
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:39,840
Thank you.

13
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,600
Zi'an.

14
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,720
Why do you like photography?

15
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:47,720
Actually, I have a problem
with forgetfulness.

16
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:50,240
Then my brother gave me my first camera

17
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,670
and told me to capture

18
00:02:51,670 --> 00:02:53,080
the beautiful moments in life.

19
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,360
That way,

20
00:02:54,390 --> 00:02:55,270
I could remember them.

21
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,520
Is it just ordinary forgetfulness?

22
00:02:58,830 --> 00:02:59,800
Not exactly.

23
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:01,190
Even though I've forgotten things,

24
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,190
I still feel like those experiences

25
00:03:03,190 --> 00:03:04,440
really happened.

26
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:06,240
As my brother puts it,

27
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,670
it's like having a dream

28
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
and forgetting everything
when you wake up.

29
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,670
It sounds like

30
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,910
your brother really cares about you.

31
00:03:15,390 --> 00:03:16,320
He does.

32
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:18,240
We've only had each other
since we were little.

33
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:19,910
He works to pay for my education.

34
00:03:20,830 --> 00:03:21,830
To be honest,

35
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:24,160
we'd give our lives for each other.

36
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,000
Ada.

37
00:03:41,390 --> 00:03:42,410
Something's not right.

38
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,440
There are consecutive gaps
in the footage from the same period.

39
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:00,390
(Zhou's Warehouse)
But no warnings were triggered,

40
00:04:00,390 --> 00:04:01,880
and there were no error messages.

41
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:04,360
Someone deliberately edited the footage.

42
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:10,460
(Strict enforcement of population
screening in the old urban village)

43
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:12,030
Ada.

44
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,360
There may have been a murder

45
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,600
near the repair shop a few days ago.

46
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,390
Something's wrong with Zhou Zi'an, too.

47
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,920
The police are moving fast.

48
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:22,640
They've already tracked down
Zhou Zicheng.

49
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,670
Be careful.

50
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:24,640
Stay alert and adapt as needed.

51
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,820
(POLICE)

52
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,760
Zhou Zicheng.

53
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:55,760
Two days ago,

54
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:57,510
Wang Guoqiang, the owner
of the neighboring shop,

55
00:04:57,510 --> 00:04:58,790
was brutally murdered.

56
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,230
We need you

57
00:05:00,230 --> 00:05:01,950
to help us with the investigation.

58
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:04,270
Come with us to the station.

59
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:05,390
Okay.

60
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:24,790
Where were you

61
00:05:24,790 --> 00:05:25,720
early that morning, two days ago?

62
00:05:26,790 --> 00:05:27,550
At the shop.

63
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:29,640
That night,

64
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,600
you had a confrontation
with Wang Guoqiang.

65
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,040
Yes.

66
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,830
Did you hit him?

67
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:37,350
Yes.

68
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,550
I killed him.

69
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:50,670
Good. Since you're willing to cooperate,

70
00:05:50,670 --> 00:05:51,950
this will be much easier.

71
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:53,110
Go ahead.

72
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:56,070
Tell us exactly
what happened that night,

73
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:58,200
leaving nothing out.

74
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,700
(Interrogation record: Wang Guoqiang
murder case, suspect: Zhou Zicheng)

75
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,160
Song Yang.

76
00:06:06,390 --> 00:06:08,160
Zhou Zi'an is still
at school and doesn't know

77
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:10,070
Zhou Zicheng has already been
taken away by the police.

78
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:11,670
This is our only chance.

79
00:06:14,110 --> 00:06:15,350
Focus on finding clues.

80
00:06:25,230 --> 00:06:26,320
(My optical sensors)

81
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,070
(have completed a full scan.)

82
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,350
(I haven't detected anything unusual.)

83
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:33,350
So many of these are illegal,
restricted products.

84
00:06:34,230 --> 00:06:35,640
I can't even identify them.

85
00:06:35,830 --> 00:06:37,350
It seems Zhou Zicheng plays

86
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:39,000
a much bigger role in this black market

87
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,720
smuggling network than we thought.

88
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:43,600
But these aren't enough
to explain all his precautions.

89
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:44,760
There must be something else.

90
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,550
(Wait.)

91
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,510
(At the one o'clock position,)

92
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,640
(there's an area with)

93
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,270
(no electromagnetic signal at all.)

94
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:55,040
No signal at all?

95
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,510
It's a signal-blocking relay.

96
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:58,720
Go check it out.

97
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,230
A Cedar memory module.

98
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:24,600
Unlike ordinary memory cards,

99
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:26,640
its capacity is several orders
of magnitude greater.

100
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,790
Song Yang.

101
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:30,000
Preparing to connect.

102
00:07:39,510 --> 00:07:40,110
Ada.

103
00:07:40,110 --> 00:07:40,880
Someone's outside.

104
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:41,760
Stay hidden.

105
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,040
(I was so focused on the memory module.)

106
00:07:48,350 --> 00:07:49,550
I only looked away
from the cameras for a moment,

107
00:07:49,550 --> 00:07:50,670
and someone's already come in.

108
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:53,920
Zhou Zicheng's shop
is quite a busy place.

109
00:07:58,390 --> 00:07:59,600
They're from the black market.

110
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,200
Ada, they're from the black market.

111
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,640
They must have seen Zhou Zicheng

112
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:06,830
being taken away by the police

113
00:08:06,950 --> 00:08:08,350
and come to destroy the evidence.

114
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,950
There are four of them.

115
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:11,600
One of them is the driver,
still in the car.

116
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,880
I can't tell if they're armed.

117
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:14,950
Be careful.

118
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:16,200
I'll find a way to help.

119
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,600
Stop wasting time.

120
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,110
While the cops are gone,

121
00:08:24,390 --> 00:08:25,790
let's take everything

122
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:26,790
we've handled.

123
00:08:26,790 --> 00:08:27,550
Got it.

124
00:08:29,390 --> 00:08:31,760
That Zhou guy has always been careful.

125
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:34,280
How did he slip up this time?

126
00:08:35,350 --> 00:08:36,110
Boss.

127
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:39,000
He didn't turn us in, did he?

128
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,590
Boss, there's a room here.

129
00:08:57,790 --> 00:08:58,440
Ada.

130
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,880
I've called the police anonymously.

131
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:00,960
The nearest patrol car

132
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:02,230
will take six minutes to arrive.

133
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,200
Hang in there.

134
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:04,280
Don't let them find you.

135
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,400
Take all this evidence away.

136
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:16,280
Once we delete our dark web accounts,

137
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,590
who could ever track us down?

138
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,640
Where did he put the stuff?

139
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,760
This definitely belongs to our company.

140
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:26,550
Boss.

141
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:29,000
But why is

142
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,200
one of these missing?

143
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:31,670
Stop talking.

144
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:33,000
Go look outside again.

145
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:40,110
Oh, no.

146
00:09:43,030 --> 00:09:44,110
Who are you people?

147
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:46,260
Don't move!

148
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:48,000
This is my home.

149
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:49,110
What do you want?

150
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:49,790
Don't move!

151
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:51,000
Stay still!

152
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:58,220
(Off the charts)

153
00:09:58,220 --> 00:09:59,100
(Emotional threshold exceeded)
Ada.

154
00:09:59,590 --> 00:10:00,400
Your emotional fluctuations

155
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,760
have exceeded the critical threshold.

156
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,640
Who are you people?

157
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:05,790
What do you want?

158
00:10:05,790 --> 00:10:06,400
Stay still!

159
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:07,640
- This is my home!
- Don't move!

160
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:08,500
What do you want?

161
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:09,760
Stay still!

162
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,650
Don't move!

163
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:12,340
Kid.

164
00:10:12,790 --> 00:10:14,200
When you get to the other side,

165
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,470
don't blame us.

166
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,230
You've only got yourself to blame.

167
00:10:17,310 --> 00:10:18,400
Instead of staying in class,

168
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:20,110
you had to skip school and come home.

169
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,590
Where's my brother?

170
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,320
You don't know yet?

171
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,120
What are you talking about?

172
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:24,730
Don't move.

173
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:25,670
What happened to my brother?

174
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,200
- Stop talking to him.
- Stay still!

175
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,030
You guys.

176
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:29,960
Get rid of him.

177
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:30,400
Yes, boss.

178
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:31,440
Let me go!

179
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,200
Let me go!

180
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,590
What happened to my brother?

181
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,520
(Ada, don't act rashly.)

182
00:10:37,230 --> 00:10:38,200
Let him go.

183
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,790
Where

184
00:10:59,790 --> 00:11:01,200
is my brother?

185
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,970
Don't do something you'll regret.

186
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:28,180
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

187
00:11:29,010 --> 00:11:33,880
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

188
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,790
♪That's me, too♪

189
00:11:38,330 --> 00:11:41,850
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

190
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:46,150
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

191
00:11:46,770 --> 00:11:50,560
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

192
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:53,410
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

193
00:11:55,350 --> 00:11:58,010
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

194
00:11:58,010 --> 00:12:00,140
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

195
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,310
♪Bring me something more?♪

196
00:12:04,010 --> 00:12:10,740
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

197
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:14,970
♪Sadness is blue♪

198
00:12:15,950 --> 00:12:19,190
♪How would you paint me?♪

199
00:12:20,190 --> 00:12:23,920
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

200
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:26,180
♪Painting without restraint♪

201
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:28,960
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

202
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:33,150
♪If I could start over♪

203
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:37,220
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

204
00:12:37,330 --> 00:12:39,970
♪Give me back my smile♪

205
00:12:40,570 --> 00:12:43,050
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

206
00:12:43,550 --> 00:12:48,790
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪
